1.1.text:
Article 5

(1) In organizing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children, the Regional Government is obliged to:

a. implement all efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence; b. provide protection for victims of violence;
c. provide recovery services and social reintegration for victims; d. encourage and increase community participation;
e. cooperate with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence; and
f. supervise the provision of services to victims involving the community.
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based violence and children;
b. facilitate the implementation of integrated services;
c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. conduct coordination and cooperation in organizing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children; and
f. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The Regional Government in carrying out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives or other persons who are legally responsible to the victim.

Article 4

(1) Every victim of gender-based violence and child victim of violence has the right to: a. obtain protection for personal security, family and property, and be free from threats relating to information to be, being, or having been given;

b. participate in the process of selecting and determining the form of protection and security support;

c. obtain information regarding case developments and court decisions;

d. obtain integrated services that are fast, appropriate, comfortable, and in accordance with needs;

e. recovery and social reintegration;

f. obtain legal assistance, psychological, spiritual guidance, economic, social and interpreter;

g. special handling related to victim confidentiality; h. obtain guarantees for their rights relating to their status as wife/mother, husband/father, child and household member as well as community member; and

i. obtain information about laws and regulations that protect victims.

(2) The Rights of Victims as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 14

Community participation as referred to in Article 8 letter e shall be carried out through:

a. providing protection for victims;
b. providing emergency assistance;
c. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding handling cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. assisting the process of submitting applications for the establishment of protection; e. conveying information to the competent authorities related to cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
f. cultivating local wisdom in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
g. conducting strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and violence against children; and
h. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and violence against children;

Article 13

Mediation, coordination and cooperation as referred to in Article 8 letter d include:

a. conducting mediation in resolving problems with related parties;
b. conducting coordination and cooperation in handling cases of violence with Provincial integrated services;
c. conducting coordination and cooperation with integrated services between regencies;
d. conducting coordination and cooperation with institutions providing services for victims of gender-based violence and violence against children; and e. conducting coordination with the Regional Government.

Article 12

Legal protection as referred to in Article 8 letter c includes: a. providing assistance in the legal process;

b. providing special legal protection for child victims of violence which may be carried out through the appointment of guardianship in accordance with applicable regulations.

Article 11

Recovery and Social Reintegration Efforts as referred to in Article 8 letter b, include:

a. providing physical recovery at health service institutions; b. providing medicolegal services;
c. assisting the return of victims;
d. providing temporary protection in safe houses (shelters); e. providing psychosocial recovery and assistance;
f. providing religious guidance services; and
g. conducting family and community preparation, economic empowerment and return to school and/or other educational institutions.

