(1) In organizing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children, the Regional Government is obliged to:

a. implement all efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence; b. provide protection for victims of violence;
c. provide recovery services and social reintegration for victims; d. encourage and increase community participation;
e. cooperate with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence; and
f. supervise the provision of services to victims involving the community.
(2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based violence and children;
b. facilitate the implementation of integrated services;
c. provide facilities and infrastructure;
d. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
e. conduct coordination and cooperation in organizing protection for victims of gender-based violence and children; and
f. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) The Regional Government in carrying out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) must pay attention to the rights and obligations of parents, guardians, husbands, wives or other persons who are legally responsible to the victim.

Article 14

Community participation as referred to in Article 8 letter e shall be carried out through:

a. providing protection for victims;
b. providing emergency assistance;
c. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding handling cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
d. assisting the process of submitting applications for the establishment of protection; e. conveying information to the competent authorities related to cases of gender-based violence and violence against children;
f. cultivating local wisdom in handling gender-based violence and violence against children;
g. conducting strengthening of community groups in handling gender-based violence and violence against children; and
h. disseminating information about laws and regulations related to gender-based violence and violence against children;

